.TH ORBLABTEST 1
.SH NAME
orblabtest \- check every Danby N-body model written as an orblab(2) script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orblabtest
[
.B -v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Orblabtest
reads the
.B SPEC
constant out of every model under
.B /appl/danby
that calls
.BR orblab->run ,
so that what is checked is the string that ships, and then checks that
the spec parses, that it has four states per body, that no rate is a NaN
at the start, and that every body's position rate is exactly its own
velocity.
.PP
The check that matters is the last.  Gravity between bodies is an
internal force, so the total momentum cannot change: summing mass times
acceleration over every body must give zero.  It does for the models
with an external term too \(em in those, the body being pushed has zero
mass and the body being held fixed has zero acceleration \(em so the one
statement covers the whole family.  A model with six bodies has fifteen
pairs and thirty reaction terms, and a sign error or a missing reaction
in any one of them breaks this sum.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/orblabtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajlabtest (1),
.IR poplabtest (1),
.IR mechlabtest (1),
.IR orblab (2)
.SH BUGS
The momentum sum is checked at the model's own starting configuration
only, not along a trajectory, so a term that is zero there and wrong
later would pass.
